82. Assigning companies to develop the zone

An area designated as an Integrated Real Estate Zone may be assigned for development in accordance with this Law and the regulation made under this Law only to one of the following parties.

(a) companies wholly owned by the Government of the Maldives, or companies in which the Government of the Maldives holds a majority share, or joint venture companies formed by the Government of the Maldives with other parties, or consortiums formed by the Government of the Maldives with other parties;

(b) companies wholly owned by Maldivians;

(c) companies wholly owned by foreigners;

(2) to a party submitting the best proposal to implement the policy determined for developing the zone, as specified in the regulation made by the Ministry under this Law;

(3) to a State-owned company, as specified in (i) of this Article.

(b) The announcement made under number (1) of (a) of this Article shall include at least the following matters.

(1) the [unclear] and total size of the Integrated Real Estate Zone;

(2) the policy determined for developing the Integrated Real Estate Zone;

(3) the guidelines for preparing the master plan setting out the proposed manner of developing the Integrated Real Estate Zone;

(4) the manner in which proposals are to be submitted, and the date and period within which proposals must be submitted.

(c) A proposal submitted under number (2) of (a) of this Article shall include at least the following matters.

(1) the plan proposed for carrying out the matters required to be done under the policy determined for developing the Integrated Real Estate Zone;

(2) the master plan setting out the proposed manner of developing the Integrated Real Estate Zone;

(3) the documents determined in the regulation made under this Law for establishing that the conditions specified in Article 83 of this Law are met;

(4) other documents and information determined in the regulation made under this Law.

(d) An Integrated Real Estate Zone may be assigned to a master developer for development under number (2) of (a) of this Article only if that party meets the conditions specified in Article 83 of this Law.

