85. Master plan

(a) An Integrated Real Estate Zone shall be developed in a manner consistent with the master plan approved by the Ministry.

(b) For the purpose of this Article, "master plan" means the physical and spatial blueprint setting out the concept and design of how the Integrated Real Estate Zone will be developed and operated.

(c) Any change to the master plan may be made by the master developer only after obtaining the approval of the Ministry as provided in this Law and the regulation made by the Ministry under this Law.

86. Master development agreement

(a) The agreement made with the master developer to whom an Integrated Real Estate Zone is assigned for development shall specify at least the following matters.

(1) the [unclear] and total size of the Integrated Real Estate Zone released to the master developer;

(2) the responsibilities the master developer must fulfil in relation to development;

(3) that there is a right to sell the leasehold rights of properties from the buildings developed in the zone as provided in this Law;

(4) that establishing all civil and municipal infrastructure of the zone is a responsibility of the master developer;

(5) the minimum standards to which urban amenities must be established, and the timeline within which those amenities must be established;

(6) the zoning permitted for land use within the zone, and the development standards;

(7) the powers vested in the master developer to subdivide land and to sublease individual plots of the zone to other developers;

(8) that there is a power to obtain loans and other credit facilities from a financial institution for developing the zone, by mortgaging the Development and Sales Rights of the zone and of the individual plots in the zone;

(9) where individual plots of the zone have been subleased to another developer, that the developer has the power to obtain loans and other credit facilities from a financial institution for developing that plot, by mortgaging the Development and Sales Rights of that plot;

(10) the consequences if the master developer breaches the agreement;

(11) other matters specified in the regulation made under this Law.

(b) The agreement signed under (a) of this Article shall be registered with the Authority as provided in this Law and the regulation made under this Law.

(c) Upon registration of the Master Development Agreement with the Authority as specified in (b) of this Article, the Authority shall issue to the master developer a leasehold certificate specifying the powers obtained by the master developer under the agreement.

(i) Upon completion of a transaction for the sale of a property being developed in an integrated zone in accordance with this Act, the [unclear] registry shall be issued by the Authority to the purchaser in the manner specified in this Act and the regulations made under this Act.

(j) The purchase of a property in an integrated real estate zone in the manner provided in this Article shall not confer on the party purchasing that property any right to become a citizen of the Maldives.

90. Responsibility to develop urban facilities

(a) Before the freehold rights of any property within an integrated real estate zone are sold or transferred, it is the responsibility of the master developer to develop that zone in a sustainable manner and to provide and complete all municipal infrastructure and social urban facilities needed for people to live there, in accordance with the standards set by the Authority in the regulations made under this Act.

(b) For the purposes of this Act, the master developer's responsibilities for establishing urban facilities shall include at least the following:

(1) a hospital providing services at general level;

(2) mosques adequate for those receiving services in the zone;

(3) shopping centres, retail shops, and cafés and restaurants;

